{"step_index":155,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:14:57Z","input_tokens":1258,"cache_read_tokens":98271,"output_tokens":671,"content":"Everything is committed. Here's what was built:\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Mobile App Structure — Complete\n\n### Navigation Architecture\n\n```\nRoot _layout.tsx  (ThemeProvider + QueryClientProvider + useProtectedRoute)\n│\n├── (auth)/              ← Stack, no header — only for unauthenticated users\n│   ├── login.tsx        ← Phone number form (react-hook-form + zod, E.164 validation)\n│   └── verify-otp.tsx  ← 6-digit box UI, resend timer, dev stub for signIn\n│\n└── (app)/               ← Protected layout: redirects to login if not authed\n    ├── profile.tsx      ← User info + role badge + sign-out\n    └── (tabs)/          ← Tabs navigator\n        ├── index.tsx    ← Role-aware dashboard (patient vs agent cards)\n        ├── referrals.tsx\n        └── wallet.tsx   ← \"Earnings\" for agents, \"Wallet\" for patients\n```\n\n### Auth Flow\n- `useAuthStore` (Zustand) hydrates from `expo-secure-store` on startup\n- Root layout's `useProtectedRoute` redirects once `isHydrated === true` — **no flash of wrong screen**\n- `(app)/_layout.tsx` has a **second-line `<Redirect />` guard** as belt-and-suspenders\n- Dev stub in `verify-otp.tsx` lets you test the full flow without a backend — it signs in with a fake token and navigates to the app immediately\n\n### Key files to wire up in Phase 3\n| File | What to do |\n|---|---|\n| [`login.tsx`](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/app/(auth)/login.tsx) | Replace `// TODO` with `useRequestOtp()` hook |\n| [`verify-otp.tsx`](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/app/(auth)/verify-otp.tsx) | Replace stub with `useVerifyOtp()` hook |\n| [`lib/api.ts`](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/lib/api.ts) | Add token refresh in the 401 interceptor |\n| [`features/auth/hooks.ts`](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/features/auth/hooks.ts) | Hooks are stubbed and typed — just uncomment the `api` calls |\n\n### To run the app now\n```bash\ncd /Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main\nnpm install       # install node_modules first\nnpx expo start    # tap into verify-otp to use the dev stub login\n```"}
{"step_index":156,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:16:10Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nHow the first complete Kezza feature should work\nInstead of building 20 screens independently, build one complete business journey from start to finish.      First end-to-end MVP journey\n1. Agent generates a referral link\n   \n   Each agent has a unique referral code.\n2. Patient registers\n   \n   The patient opens the link, verifies their mobile number and creates an account.\n3. Referral is linked\n   \n   The backend connects the patient's account with the referring agent and locks the attribution.\n4. Patient purchases a treatment\n   \n   Kezza verifies the actual collected payment.\n5. Patient receives rewards\n   \n   The backend credits eligible points to the patient's points ledger.\n6. Agent receives commission\n   \n   The backend determines the agent's commission tier and records the commission.\n7. Both see their results\n   \n   The patient sees treatment credit; the agent sees earnings and referral details.  This one workflow tests the entire foundation: authentication, referral attribution, sales, points, commissions, database and mobile API integration.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-13T11:46:10+05:30.\n\nThe user's current state is as follows:\nOther open documents:\n- /Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/src/app/_layout.tsx (LANGUAGE_UNSPECIFIED)\n- /Users/ravi/Desktop/Kezza_mobile-main/backend/app/main.py (LANGUAGE_UNSPECIFIED)\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
